-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Exolon
  Publisher   Hewson Consultants, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Exolon (1987)(Hewson Consultants)(128K).z80
  MD5         87515df87645c4179a9ef90663774c7f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Approved painted figures; pixel borders and original foreground
              occlusion retained. Optional, off by default. Native editable
              81-frame sheet. Source: Enhanced colours: Jao Paulo (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Note        Exact 128K release with AY sound. Original figure colours by
              default; optional approved Enhanced figure colours, off by
              default. Original loading screen. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues:
              individual update and beeper pulse timing vary with video
              contention; measured pace stays within 2%. Sound deadline uses a
              working CTC channel 3; missing-clock fallback preserves
              operation but has no timing acceptance. Missing: natural
              completion, later-zone exhaustive playthrough, hardware and
              other-emulator tests.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite ammo
   3  Infinite grenades
   4  Mines harmless
   5  Immunity

  Five archive options verified independently against this 128K release:
  lives, ammo, grenades, mines harmless, immunity. All off by default.
  Unverified conflicting enemy-control options excluded.

